s7-6-p24 = realized (prose (cons "For an initially empty \(P\to Q\) queue, let \(N\) and \(D\) count successful sends and receives. The inductive invariant is \(N=D+|u|\), hence \(D\le N\): a send increments both \(N\) and \(|u|\), a receive increments \(D\) and decrements \(|u|\), and the other cases preserve all three. It is a property of the **composed program**, not an assumption about the individual processes. Trace projection and reconstruction follow by induction over the same cases, subject to FIFO matching and scheduling constraints. Neither fairness nor eventual delivery follows from the transition rules. Changing the network handler to permit loss, duplication, or reordering changes the composite state and invariant accordingly. The queue is a chosen example of an interaction cut, not a privileged architectural boundary." nil)) (cons "par-sends" (cons "par-recvs" (cons "par-count" (cons "par-D-le-N" nil))))
